.TH wallstreet 1 "16 November 2026" wallstreet "wallstreet"
.SH NAME
wallstreet \- fill your console with wallstreet melodrama technobabble

.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBwallstreet\fP

.SH DESCRIPTION

This utility will fill your console with Wall Street technobabble.

It splits a \fBtmux\fP(1) (or \fBbyobu\fP(1)) window into panes of news and statistics, like any good computer screen on Wall Street: a table of the most active stocks, three scrolling tickers (gainers, losers, headlines), a feed reader and news pictures as ASCII art.

The data is real.  Quotes come from the Nasdaq market movers API, headlines and pictures from the RSS feeds listed in \fIshare/wallstreet/newsboat.urls\fP.  Results are cached for a short time in the temporary directory.

To quit, press Ctrl-C in any pane.

.SH SEE ALSO
\fBtmux\fP(1), \fBbyobu\fP(1), \fBnewsboat\fP(1)

.SH AUTHOR
